      "id": "current_http_error_normalization",
      "cause": "The platform can bypass post_process_code on HTTP errors. The evaluator consequently treated the current cards.list HTTP 404 / FB_IVR_CHANNEL_102 WARNING as a missing result and transferred to an agent.",
      "repair": "Snapshot and explicitly clear the relevant transport-result fields before each list request. Recover only the documented no-card warning from a fresh failure counter and the current response namespace. Preserve technical-error handling for other statuses, malformed bodies, timeouts and stale responses.",
      "sources": [
        "sources/documents/2026-10-01-service-contract.md §§3–4",
        "sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md §§2–3",
        "OBSERVED LIVE FAILURES: STRESS05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "detour_resumption",
      "cause": "The outside node extracted only an intent. Valid card digits were lost, and its evaluator required a menu yes/no even when the customer clearly resumed the interrupted task.",
      "repair": "Extract the same primitive task information during the detour. Restore the saved question and its budget, then replay an in-scope answer exactly once. A yes to the menu question remains menu consent and can never authorize a bank write. Incidental small talk is an unanswered task question rather than an unrelated banking request.",
      "sources": [
        "sources/meetings/2026-10-07-analysis-session-transcript.txt 00:10:54–00:12:20",
        "sources/emails/2026-10-09-decisions-recap.txt points 2–3",
        "OBSERVED LIVE FAILURES: STRESS12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "literal_card_name_extraction",
      "cause": "The extractor correctly produced the customer’s literal product name, but the 0.65 confidence threshold discarded it. The deterministic ineligible-card branch therefore never received the name.",
      "repair": "Use a 0.4 confidence threshold for literal card-name capture and explicitly require capture regardless of eligibility or whether the name was offered. Eligibility, ownership and uniqueness remain deterministic checks against the loaded card list.",
      "sources": [
        "sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md §3.3",
        "OBSERVED LIVE FAILURES: EXTRA05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "confirmation_reference_is_not_necessarily_correction",
      "cause": "Any extracted card name triggered reselection, including a fresh explicit confirmation naming the already selected card. This erased the email challenge and currency, repeated the balance lookup and prevented sending. Earlier stages also omitted follow-up fields, and actual card corrections discarded correlated email terms.",
      "repair": "Resolve references against the loaded list before deciding whether they change the selected card. A unique reference to the current card preserves the challenge; different, unmatched or ambiguous references cannot authorize it. Preserve email currency, period and destination restrictions through actual card corrections, reload the new card and obtain fresh confirmation. Capture these terms in the another-card and offer stages.",
      "sources": [
        "sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md §§3.3, 6–7",
        "sources/documents/2026-10-01-service-contract.md §§5.4–5.7",
        "OBSERVED LIVE FAILURES: EXTRA08"
      ]
    }
